<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13069"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 11:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes tne Pastor has nelped me a lot a nr as the Deten&#42;ion Chaplain. The j help sniedtn ouittre hare bimp. tnat un innate en co intris. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s part English, part German, part French and part Latin. <BR> <BR> <BR>This actually makes me wonder if his Sentax was as bad as we thought or if the transposer&#40;...lator&#41; just omitted the words they couldn&#39;t read. Apparently the alphabet doesn&#39;t come under the heading of &#34;things that must be kept tidy and in their proper place&#34; in Denny&#39;s world.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
