<!--Post: 13144--><!--Time: 1114306599-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13144"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 6:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop, <BR> <BR>I have read one book on handwriting analysis and imo it is as objective as a lie detector test or hypnosis.  .  .   <BR> <BR>If I am not mistaken more writing analysts are being subject to lawsuit when their &#34;opnions&#34; cause harm to an accused.  .  .   <BR> <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
