<!--Post: 13147--><!--Time: 1114308067-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13147"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 7:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, When we must have the attention we think we deserve. Since we can&#39;t send puzzles or threats to the media or the police we have to resort to letter writing. I agree Tac. As you know I make is a point to study text, and writing. Writing anaysis is opinion based because there is no way to prove that  a person was thinking or feeling a certain way at a certain time. &#40;IE differences in the way he write a word when he is angry or rushed as opposed to Happy&#41; They can only guess. But since he is writing letters. It shows he may now be harboring some guilt and searching for forgiveness. That is what I wanted. I prayed for him to develop emotions while in jail. So he could see wht he did to so many lives. I how he feels bad, and does for a very long time. I doubt if he will find too many people to feel sorry for him.   Thanks Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13147-->
<!--Post: 13157--><!--Time: 1114375436-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13157"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 24, 2005 - 1:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Em <BR> <BR>You have a good soul. Forgiveness is the basis of civilization but forgiveness is much easier when it is not your child who is the victim.  <BR> <BR>Unfortunately for the Rader&#39;s of the world we do not have the knowledge to rehabilatate them. Like a child molester or rapist, the fact remains that if they are released they are a solid bet to offend again.  .  .  <BR> <BR>I believe that we will not be able to help these people until we unlock more of the mysteries of the brain. <BR> <BR>Until that point our society needs to acknowledge that we can NOT rehab these lost souls. <BR> <BR>Instead of rehabilitation we must use a &#34;substitute&#34; for them. I believe that virtual reality technology and robotics hold the key to substituting the stimulus these offenders crave.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Creating a robotic/doll or object could act as a outlet for a pedephile or rapist when the &#34;urge&#34; hits. Virtual reality technology could create a &#34;video&#34; game that allows the same type of &#34;outlet&#34;.  <BR> <BR>All I know is that what we are doing now is NOT working.  .  .   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13157-->
<!--Post: 13158--><!--Time: 1114408265-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13158"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 24, 2005 - 10:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->TAC said; &#34;All I know is that what we are doing now is NOT working. . .&#34;. <BR> <BR>I totally agree, Tac. That&#39;s why I created the &#34;Preventing Future BTKs&#34; thread &#40;under &#34;General&#34;&#41;. I&#39;ll post the rest of my response there, where it&#39;s more appropriate.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
