<!--Post: 13280--><!--Time: 1114766892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13280"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 2:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.wichitanewsbrief.com/newsletter.aspx?id=recent" target=_top>http://www.wichitanewsbrief.com/newsletter.aspx?id =recent</a> <BR> <BR>is this the letter Tom got hold of? <BR> <BR>&#34;BTK:  MY PEN PAL <BR>  <BR>It&#39;s a claim a west coast woman can make after receiving a four page letter from Dennis Rader from his jail cell here in Wichita.  The woman thought that she would send him a letter, and did not know what to expect.  She was floored when she got a response, and that it was so long.  In the letter, he talks about how much he has relied upon his pastor and the jail&#39;s chaplain.  He also talks about his daily routine, and expresses that receiving any mail &#34;expressing Christian concerns for him and his family&#34; is a welcome perk.&#34; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
